# PROPOSAL — mqtt-ingress ACL for ADR-0032 Path B. NOT applied. Reference only.
# Username = client-cert CN (use_identity_as_username true). Each tenant may
# publish ONLY to its own SparkPlug group's DATA subtree, and may NOT write any
# command topic. See docs/ingestion/mqtt-ingress-design.md §3.1 (A2/A3/A7).
#
# Default (no matching user line): deny. Mosquitto denies topics not granted.

# ── CPACK (client cert CN=CPACK) ──────────────────────────────────────────────
user CPACK
topic write spBv1.0/CPACK/NBIRTH/#
topic write spBv1.0/CPACK/NDATA/#
topic write spBv1.0/CPACK/NDEATH/#
topic write spBv1.0/CPACK/DBIRTH/#
topic write spBv1.0/CPACK/DDATA/#
topic write spBv1.0/CPACK/DDEATH/#
# Explicit deny is implicit (no grant) — CPACK cannot write DCMD/NCMD nor any
# other tenant's subtree. No read grants: an ingress publisher never subscribes.

# ── INCOPLAST (client cert CN=INCOPLAST) ──────────────────────────────────────
user INCOPLAST
topic write spBv1.0/INCOPLAST/NBIRTH/#
topic write spBv1.0/INCOPLAST/NDATA/#
topic write spBv1.0/INCOPLAST/NDEATH/#
topic write spBv1.0/INCOPLAST/DBIRTH/#
topic write spBv1.0/INCOPLAST/DDATA/#
topic write spBv1.0/INCOPLAST/DDEATH/#

# NOTE: the bridge connection authenticates internally to `mosquitto:1883`
# (loopback, allow_anonymous) — it is NOT an external user and needs no ACL
# entry here; command topics are excluded at the bridge `topic` lines, not here.
